        <body text=#000000 bgcolor=#4acbd6>
                <div id="pagestyle">
                <div id="contenttype">
                        <tbody>
                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666" style="table-layout: fixed; margin:5px 0;" >
                                                <tr height="25px" class="bgcolor" style="height:25px;width:100%;background:#e6e6e6;">
                                                        <td style="padding-left:20px;" >
                                                                <span class="help-header">
                                                                        Maintenance
                                                                </span>
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
                                                                                                 
                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666" style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;">                                                                                             
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        Administration 
                                                                </span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;There are only one account that can access  Web-Management interface. It is admin. Admin has read/write access privilege. In this web page, you can set new password for admin.
                                                                </span>
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
                                                                                                                            
                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666" style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"   >                                                                                                  
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        Time Zone
                                                                </span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;The system time is the time used by the device for scheduling services.You can manually set the time or connect to a NTP (Network Time Protocol) server.If an NTP server is set, you will only need to set the time zone.If you manually set the time, you may also set Daylight Saving dates and the system time will automatically adjust on those dates.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
                                                                                                                                         
                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666"  style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"  >                                                                                                              
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        Firmware
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		Firmware::Firmware Upgrade 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;You can upgrade the firmware of the router in this page. Make sure the firmware you want to use is on the local hard drive of the computer. Click on Browse to browse the local hard drive and locate the firmware to be used for the update.
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		Firmware::Restore Configuration 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;The current system settings can be saved as a file onto the local hard drive.The saved file or any other saved setting file can be loaded back on the router.To reload a system settings file, click on Browse to browse the local hard drive and locate the system file
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;to be used. You may also reset the router back to factory settings by clicking on Restore.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>

                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666"  style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"  >
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        SysRestart
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		SysRestart::Reboot 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;To restart system with current settings.
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		SysRestart::Reset 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;To restart system with factory default settings.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>

                                <div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666" style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"   >
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        Diagnostics
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		Diagnostics::Diagnostic Test 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;Shows the test results for the connectivity of the physical layer and protocol layer for both LAN and WAN sides.
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		Diagnostics::Trace Route Test 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;Shows the test results for the data path from ONT to the url/IP. It can also be used to locate network problems.
                                                                </span><br>
																<span class="help-sub">
																		Diagnostics::TcpDump Test 
																</span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;Capture data packets of a certain interface, such as PON, WiFi or LAN port.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
								<div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666"  style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"  >
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        WiFi Timer
                                                                </span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;You can make a WiFi Timer schedule during which WiFi will be opened. WiFi will be turned off beyond the configured time period to reduce radiation.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
								<div id="block1">
                                        <table cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width="666"  style="padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"  >
                                                <tr>
                                                        <td style="text-align:justify;text-justify:auto;">
                                                                <span class="help-main">
                                                                        Reboot Timer
                                                                </span><br>
                                                                <span class="help-text">
                                                                        &nbsp;&nbsp;Reboot Timer is used to reboot ONT at a certain time to keep ONT working in a smooth state.
                                                                </span> 
                                                        </td>
                                                </tr>
                                        </table>
                                </div>
                        </tbody>
                        </div>
                </div>

                        
        </body>
</html>
